Author Max Beaty:

I created two python files (ShareScreen and ShareService)

ShareScreen: Builds the screen interface that allows the customer to enter their email in
There are some checks in there to make sure that it is an email being entered in.
It will send when selected send or for Keyboard (enter) 
There is also a skip feature that just removes the page.

[IMPORTANT]Flet is imported and needs to be installed before testing.
the cmd to install is : python3 -m pip install flet

ShareService is built to interact with the api. it opens and upload the stats and the video
there is some error checking for instance if the stats/video were unable to be opened or if the there it freezes.
ShareService was built to test and to later deploy. Mock can be set to True when testing or False when it actually needs to pull files from the API
I tried to comment as best I could the things that needed to be changed for Prod

[THE ULTIMATE TEST]
To go a step further with my testing I found a precoded api that I went through and tailored it to work with this project. I had "putt.api" folder containing api.py. I then created a key using resend.com and used my local pc as an acting server by running:

[CMD_to_run]
export RESEND_API_KEY="what the Key was"
python3 -m uvicorn api:app --reload --port 8000

on the the Email_forwarding_Feature I set I ran 
python3 main.py

After this I entered in my email to the interface that was created in ShareScreen and then recieved an email.

[side_note]:
Also to mention I added two example files in the ShareService "putt_stats.json" and "putt.mp4" these were just used to test if I could recieve them in the email.

The email that came through after the test contained what was expected!